{
  "about": "Every surface a writer can see, for scripts/dev/capture.mjs. Each surface has a stable id (screenshots and decisions refer to it), the pattern family it belongs to, and the steps that open it from a fresh page. `presets` are shared step lists. Steps: open, goto, click (force), dblclick, rightclick, hover, focus, fill, press, type, command (run a ⌘K command by title), menuItem (choose an item in a native menu, see tauri-mock.js), scroll, wait, waitFor, eval, reload; any step can be optional. `root` names the surface's own element (an overlay), which scripts/dev/measure.mjs measures. `menu: true` also saves the native menu the surface pops up as JSON. `seed` adds files and preferences to the mock; `routes` answers off-site requests with fixtures. `unreachable` lists what the mock cannot show, and why.",
